  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cash Consortium of Sudan (CCS) Extension</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Phase 1: On behalf of the Cash Consortium of Sudan (CCS), Mercy Corps requests GBP 5,000,000 from FCDO to establish an effective, efficient and people-centred response to the complex humanitarian emergency in Sudan. The CCS will reach an estimated 232,560 individuals across 19 localities in 9 states with a harmonised and scaled approach to multi-sectoral cash assistance for basic needs. Targeted locations include both the worst conflict-affected areas, as well as displacement hot spots, with a focus on hotspot areas with IPC4, included in the Sudan Famine Prevention Plan 2024, namely Khartoum, Central, West, East and South Darfur, and North, South and West Kordofan, and Gezira. Phase 2: Extension of the CCS programme with CARE working in Gezira, Khartoum, S.Kordofan providing MPCA and GCTs</narrative>
  </description>
